-- title:
--   Degree of the kernel under Xᵢ ↦ Xᵢ^q
-- statement:
--   Let $B$ be a commutative ring and let $\varphi$ be an element of `Series B`, that is a pair $\varphi = (\varphi_0,\varphi_1)$ of power series in $B[[X_0,X_1]]$ indexed by `Fin 2`. Assume `FormalODModule.HasKernelOfDegree φ d` for a natural number $d$: the quotient algebra `KerAlgebra φ` $= B[[X_0,X_1]]/(\varphi_0,\varphi_1)$, the quotient by the ideal generated by the range of $\varphi$, is finite as a $B$-module, is projective as a $B$-module, and for every field $\kappa$ (in the same universe as $B$) and every ring homomorphism $f : B \to \kappa$ the $\kappa$-vector space $\kappa[[X_0,X_1]]/(f\varphi_0, f\varphi_1)$, obtained by applying $f$ to the coefficients of $\varphi$, has $\kappa$-dimension $d$. Let $q$ be a natural number with $q \neq 0$. The conclusion is that the pair obtained from $\varphi$ by the substitution $X_i \mapsto X_i^{q}$, namely `φ.comp fun i => X i ^ q` whose $i$-th entry is $\varphi_i(X_0^{q}, X_1^{q})$, satisfies `FormalODModule.HasKernelOfDegree` with degree $d \cdot q^{2}$: the algebra $B[[X_0,X_1]]/(\varphi_0(X^{q}),\varphi_1(X^{q}))$ is again finite and projective over $B$, and all its field-valued fibres have dimension $d q^{2}$.
--
--   This is the multiplicativity of the degree of a finite locally free kernel under the $q$-power Frobenius-type substitution on the two-dimensional formal affine space, the case needed when a $\varpi$- or Frobenius-power is factored through $X_i \mapsto X_i^{q}$. It is used in the rigidity arguments for homomorphisms of formal $\mathcal{O}_D$-modules and in the comparison of rigidifications of fake elliptic curves in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd part of the development.
